# Infomaniak API credentials for certbot's DNS-01 challenge.
#
# SETUP
#   1. Copy this file to `infomaniak.ini` (same directory). It is gitignored.
#   2. Create a token at https://manager.infomaniak.com -> Users and profile -> My profile -> Developer -> API tokens
#      Create token, with scopes "Domain" and "Domain write". Paste it below.
#   3. chmod 600 nginx/certbot/infomaniak.ini
#      certbot refuses to run if this file is group/world readable.
#
# SECURITY — read this once
#   A "Domain"-scoped token can rewrite ANY DNS record on your Infomaniak
#   account, including MX. Its blast radius is larger than the certificates it
#   exists to obtain: someone holding it can redirect your mail or issue certs
#   for your domains anywhere. Treat it as your most sensitive credential here.
#   If you want to shrink that exposure, delegate only the challenge record —
#   CNAME _acme-challenge.<domain> to a throwaway zone — so this token has no
#   authority over your real records.

dns_infomaniak_token = paste-your-infomaniak-api-token-here
